WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.315
(intense music)

00:00:01.315 --> 00:00:05.135
- The Harvard Brain Bank is
one of the largest brain banks

00:00:05.135 --> 00:00:06.356
in the country.

00:00:06.356 --> 00:00:10.523
At the moment we house
approximately 5,000 brain specimens.

00:00:16.568 --> 00:00:19.943
My name is Sabina Berretta,
I am the scientific director

00:00:19.943 --> 00:00:22.350
of the Harvard Brain
Tissue Resource Center,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.969
which we affectionately
call the Harvard Brain Bank.

00:00:25.969 --> 00:00:28.817
Our mission is to collect brain specimens,

00:00:28.817 --> 00:00:32.879
store them, categorize them, and
then redistribute them out

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:37.115
to investigators across
the world that do research

00:00:37.115 --> 00:00:39.797
on the human brain, and in particular,

00:00:39.797 --> 00:00:42.638
on large number of
neurological and psychiatric

00:00:42.638 --> 00:00:46.555
brain disorders, such as
schizophrenia, bipolar disorder,

00:00:46.555 --> 00:00:49.805
Parkinson, Huntington, and many others.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.809
The Brain Bank never sleeps,

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:56.976
we have two sets of people
that are on call 24/7,

00:00:57.822 --> 00:00:59.976
we have a very limited time window

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:02.537
from when the person passes away

00:01:02.537 --> 00:01:06.721
to the time we need to be done
with this whole processing.

00:01:06.721 --> 00:01:09.200
- So this is gonna be your first
brain late at night, right?

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.357
- I know, first late night brain.

00:01:11.357 --> 00:01:14.715
- We have to do it in less than 24 hours.

00:01:14.715 --> 00:01:17.476
Our courier will bring
it to McLean Hospital

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.021
to the brain bank.

00:01:19.021 --> 00:01:20.205
- [Voiceover] So just put it out here,

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:22.705
so we're gonna take ourselves.

00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:32.542
- There will be a dissectionist
ready to dissect the brain.

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:38.533
That involves, so separating
the two hemispheres,

00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:41.212
one of the two hemispheres
is put in a solution

00:01:41.212 --> 00:01:45.520
that preserves it, the other
hemisphere will be dissected

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.187
in thick sections, and
those will be frozen.

00:01:50.842 --> 00:01:53.723
We are not even close to understand

00:01:53.723 --> 00:01:56.971
a lot of what we take for granted.

00:01:56.971 --> 00:02:01.730
Our thoughts, our instincts,
our feelings, our emotions.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.135
There are a lot of questions
we still don't know,

00:02:04.135 --> 00:02:06.408
and a lot of our brain functions

00:02:06.408 --> 00:02:10.673
still will probably be studied
for a long time to come.

00:02:10.673 --> 00:02:13.640
A brain donation is,
in a very concrete way,

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:18.274
a gift of knowledge and it
cannot be done without the help

00:02:18.274 --> 00:02:21.274
of families and people
willing to donate their brain.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.857
(gentle music)

